KZ3 patch 1116 (SPU pass 101): host frames for guest setjmp/longjmp. A lifted guest longjmp restored the guest
registers and then returned to its lifted caller (KZ3: longjmp 0xABBD8C back into luaD_throw 0x9EE30, so a caught
Lua error ran on as if none happened). The lifter's --setjmp ADDR[:STATUS_OFF] / --longjmp ADDR (or `setjmp ADDR
[status=OFF]` / `longjmp ADDR` rows in the --overrides file) make every `bl` to a setjmp a PPU_SJ_CALL (a host setjmp
recorded per thread under the guest jmp_buf, r1 and host frame) and emit each longjmp as <name>__ljbody plus a wrapper
that host-longjmps to the matching record (frameless _setjmp(buf, NULL) on MinGW x64), restoring the dispatch-depth
and vcall-sp counters at the landing; no record = the old return, logged. Log `[ljmp] caught status=N (#count ...)`.
KZ3_LJMP=0 = the old behaviour. Host test tools/spu/test_r101_setjmp.sh. Notes the RE notes Pass 101.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): `setjmp_marks` after upstream's `insn_patches` in the worker signature; PPU_MM_SNAP after the body opening.

